WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.560
Fans of the game might have a&nbsp;
+5 resistance to charm spells,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.780
but are they charmed by "Dungeons &amp; Dragons: Honor&nbsp;
Among Thieves"? Here's what they have to say.

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:15.540
What a good time it is to be a Dungeons &amp; Dragons&nbsp;
fan. 23 years after Courtney Solomon's critically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:21.944
panned D&amp;D movie relegated the RPG classic's&nbsp;
live-action adaptations to direct-to-DVD status,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.944 --> 00:00:27.120
"Dungeons &amp; Dragons: Honor Among Thieves"&nbsp;
has captured the best things about D&amp;D. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.080
arrived on the big screen with the kind of&nbsp;
joy and adventure that bodes well for future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:36.600
sequels. Critics and audiences rate Jonathan&nbsp;
Goldstein and John Francis Daley's movie highly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.200
and the likable cast makes for a&nbsp;
magnificent party of adventurers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.360
All of this is extremely good publicity for&nbsp;
the game, and it doesn't exactly hurt that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:50.393
Pine thinks everyone should play D&amp;D. But&nbsp;
what do actual players think of the movie?

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.020
"Sounds lovely."

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:52.800
"Quite the opposite."

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.480
"I know. I was being ironic."

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.840
"I find irony is a blade that cuts he&nbsp;
who wields it and most especially."

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.400
Turns out, many of them really enjoy it,&nbsp;
and they've taken to the game's subreddit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.120
to express their joy. In a post that&nbsp;
proclaimed their love for "Honor Among&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.020
Thieves," one redditor described their&nbsp;
experience in the theater, writing,

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:14.280
"The audience tonight were all geeks&nbsp;
(surprise!) and so the energy of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:17.820
theater was really up-beat. There&nbsp;
were even tear-jerker moments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:22.012
which I must give them props for since&nbsp;
that's hard to do in a 'high fantasy' film!"

00:01:22.012 --> 00:01:26.754
Another subreddit member found the communal&nbsp;
viewing experience similarly comfortable.

00:01:26.754 --> 00:01:30.120
"It was a pretty full theater&nbsp;
which I was shocked about and I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.460
didn't hear a single person complaining about it."

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:36.720
Apart from the positive experience of&nbsp;
seeing the film with fellow enthusiasts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:42.954
several D&amp;D aficionados have excitedly pointed&nbsp;
out specific details and references in the movie.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.400
"What is that again?"

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:45.720
"It's an owlbear."

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.040
They were particularly impressed by its&nbsp;
emotional impact, but the experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:54.720
of simply being able to see the movie as a&nbsp;
longtime D&amp;D fan is also important to many.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.920
Another point of discussion in the subreddit&nbsp;
were about the way "Dungeons &amp; Dragons:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:04.740
Honor Among Thieves" manages to marry its comedic&nbsp;
moments with its more heartfelt ones. One Redditor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.880
compared the movie's vibe to James Gunn's&nbsp;
work in the Marvel Cinematic Universe, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.680
has been known to balance a similar line between&nbsp;
laughter and emotional gut punches. They wrote,

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.300
"It's a D&amp;D fantasy Guardians of the&nbsp;
Galaxy film, feel it's the best way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.560
summarize it. It's not a comedy but there's&nbsp;
definitely some good comedy and character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:26.700
writing with the jokes. There is also some&nbsp;
genuine heart in it that makes you care."

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.320
Another Redditor agreed, complimenting the&nbsp;
movie's successful balance between the serious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:36.713
and humorous moments, and compared "Honor Among&nbsp;
Thieves" favorably to recent superhero movies.

00:02:36.774 --> 00:02:41.160
"Better than the last 4 or 5 Marvel&nbsp;
and DC outings. Comedy was done well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.480
it managed to take itself seriously when&nbsp;
it needed to and joked when appropriate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.980
without marvel level 'he's right behind me&nbsp;
isn't he' detracting from serious moments."

00:02:50.407 --> 00:02:51.960
"Follow me to the orifice."

00:02:53.814 --> 00:02:54.891
"The orifice?"

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.040
Though it's clear that fans appreciate&nbsp;
the movie's comedy-drama balance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.820
it seems that the best part of watching&nbsp;
the film was still being able to share the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.240
experience with their fellow players&nbsp;
— to the point that even the movie's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.600
occasional lower moments couldn't&nbsp;
rain on the parade. One fan wrote,

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.220
"It wasn't perfect, but the fact that everyone&nbsp;
I went with to see it, which included 4 out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:18.840
6 of my players and most of our children (a&nbsp;
total of 9 of us), were standing around and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:24.240
talking about it and it took us all about 15-20&nbsp;
minutes to leave the theater, is quite telling."

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.560
They continued to say,

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:29.049
"Plus we were talking with other random&nbsp;
people in the theater that loved it as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.049 --> 00:03:33.399
well. I haven't felt that excited post&nbsp;
movie since like the first Matrix."

00:03:33.399 --> 00:03:35.619
Another user chimed in to say,

00:03:35.619 --> 00:03:41.220
"If you are a fan of the game you will love this&nbsp;
movie. Will everyone love this movie? No. I can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:46.320
see certain demos not wanting to rush out to&nbsp;
see this. But if you like D&amp;D it's a slam dunk."

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:50.880
This emotional experience alone is clearly&nbsp;
enough to score "Dungeons &amp; Dragons: Honor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.500
Among Thieves" some serious appreciation points&nbsp;
from the fandom. The fact that it also happens&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.667
to be a genuinely good, fun adventure&nbsp;
movie probably doesn't hurt, either.

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:01.706
"Anything you want to add?"

00:04:02.462 --> 00:04:03.427
"I'm good."

